# Don't ship dev/test files into the production image.
#
# Docker matches with filepath.Match semantics, where `*` does not cross `/`. A bare
# `__pycache__/` therefore matched only the context root, so src/__pycache__ and
# src/siseli_local_bridge/__pycache__ shipped in every locally built image -- changing the
# layer hash, so two developers building the same commit got different images. Every
# pattern below that can occur at depth carries a `**/` prefix for that reason.
.git/
.gitignore
tests/

# Build, test and coverage residue. None of it is tracked, so a clean checkout never
# has any of it and CI cannot notice its absence -- tests/test_packaging.py asserts
# these patterns directly rather than inspecting a built image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.egg-info/
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Documentation. CHANGELOG.md is re-included deliberately: Supervisor renders the
# add-on's own copy on the Changelog tab, and test_packaging.py treats it as
# canonical. DOCS.md is not re-included -- Supervisor reads the Documentation tab
# from the repository checkout, not from the image.
*.md
!CHANGELOG.md
